# NOTICE

## This corpus is published for educational purposes

**harness-atlas is a research and teaching instrument.** It exists to make agent
harnesses legible side by side — to show how they can be decomposed, what a
primitive is, and where systems genuinely differ. It is course material and
reference reading, not a buyer's guide, not a procurement input, and not advice.

**It is not an endorsement, a ranking, or a recommendation of any product.** The
scorecard states this on its face: nine of its ten axes are *positions*, not
scores, and neither end of an axis is better than the other. Exactly one dimension
is admitted as graded, and it says so.

**Nothing here has been signed off by a human reviewer.** Every profile carries
`status: DRAFT`, and every scorecard card and deep-read document carries a
**drafted-until-verified** banner naming the model that drafted it and the date.
That banner comes off only when a person re-reads the page and signs it. Until
then, treat every claim as a reading to be checked against the vendor's own
sources — which are cited on every page for exactly that purpose.

**Read anything load-bearing at the source.** Each page records the version it was
read at and the date. Harnesses in this space ship weekly; a page that was true at
its capture may be false today, and the corpus says so rather than pretending
otherwise.

